          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, V 1.
            ).
          #LTTopologyAsSubobject.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    J \hookrightarrow \Omega
            %p
              satisfying three conditions. This perspective gives the direct relation to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topologies"} Grothendieck topologies
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#RelationToGrothendieckTopology"} below
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Equivalently, the third axiom in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LTTopologyDef"}
              can be replaced with the (internal) statement that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is order-preserving.
            %p
              The equivalence amounts to the fact that, within the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topoi"} topoi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth+values"} truth values
              is in fact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong
              (a special case of the fact that, for an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
              on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} monoidal closed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensorial+strength"} tensorial strengths
              are the same as
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enrichments
              %em automatically
              preserves finite meets.
            %p
              Thus, a Lawvere-Tierney topology is the same thing as an internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
              on the preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              (aka, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+closure"} Moore closure
              on the one-element set), which amounts to the same thing as a natural closure operator on subobjects.
            %p
              Specifically, given any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \hookrightarrow Y
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+morphism"} characteristic morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_X: Y \to \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \circ \chi_X
              is another morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_*(X)
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_*(X)
              are those elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              that are ‘locally’ in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #TheClosureOperator.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closure+operator"} closure operator
              induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\overline{(-)}_X : Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
            %p
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              lattice of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Hom
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Ω
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi Sub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom(X, \Omega) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; Sub(X)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{Hom(1,j)}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\overline{(-)}}}
                    \\\
                    Hom(X,\Omega) &amp;\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}&amp; Sub(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              This means that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi char
                      %mi U
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} char U : X \to \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi char
                    %mover
                      %mi U
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi char
                        %mi U
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi j
                    %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    char \overline{U} : X \stackrel{char U}{\to} \Omega \stackrel{j}{\to} \Omega
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "\nMacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, p. 220
            ).
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              is a Lawvere-Tierney topology, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LTTopologyDef"}
              precisely if the corresponding closure operator, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheClosureOperator"}
              satisfies for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, Y \in E
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subset \overline{A}
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mover
                            %mi A
                            %mo ¯
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\overline{A}} = \overline{A}
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi B
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo =
                        %mover
                          %mi A
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ∩
                        %mover
                          %mi B
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{A \cap B} = \overline{A} \cap \overline{B}
                  \.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, V 1., prop 1
            ).
          %h3#sheaves Sheaves
          %p
            Using Lawvere–Tierney topologies, the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
            generalizes from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topoi
            to arbitrary topoi.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            with Lawvere-Tierney topology
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LTTopologyDef"}
            and associated closure operator
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{(-)} : Sub(-) \to Sub(-)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheClosureOperator"}
          #DenseMonos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A subobject
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in Sub(X)
              is called
              %strong dense
              if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi U
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo =
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{U} = X
            %p
              The corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+monomorphism"} dense monomorphism
          #JSheaf.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              An object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in E
              is called a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              if it is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              with respect to the dense monomorphisms.
            %p
              This means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              = succeed "-sheaf" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \hookrightarrow X
              the induced morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(X,F) \to Hom(U,F)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+presheaf"} separated presheaf
              if this morphism is itself a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
          %p
            This is for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk, p. 223
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#SheafSubtoposes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            \-Sheaf subtoposes
          #RelationToCoveringSieves.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              a Lawvere-Tierney topology on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sh_j(E) \hookrightarrow E
            %p
              of
              %a{:href => "#JSheaf"} j-sheaves
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+embedding"} geometric embedding
            %p
              So in particular
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_j(E)
              is itself a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              and the embedding is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
              which has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} left exact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              functor
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to Sh_j(E)
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              functor.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"}> MacLaneMoerdijk V 3., theorem 1
            ).
          %h3#RelationToGrothendieckTopology Equivalence with Grothendieck topologies
          #RelationToCoveringSieves.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E := [C^{op}, Set]
              its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              are equivalent to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topologies
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              is the presheaf that assigns to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in C
              the set of all
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} sieve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Sieves
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Omega : U \mapsto Sieves_C(U)
                    \\,.
            %p since we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sieves
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Sub
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sieves_C (U)=Sub_E(y(U))=hom(y(U),\Omega)=\Omega(U)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \hookrightarrow \Omega
              is therefore precisely a choice of a collection of sieves on each object, which is closed under pullback. The proof therefore amounts to checking that the condition that such a collection of sieves is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is equivalent to the statement that the characteristic map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \hookrightarrow \Omega
              (see remark
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LTTopologyAsSubobject"}
          %p Here is more discussion of this point:
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a small site. Then given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subpresheaf"} subpresheaf
            inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \hookrightarrow G
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Set^{C^\op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is locally in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (that is,
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in j_*(F)(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} covering family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = (c_i: U_i \to X)_i
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c^*(f)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            is in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            (that is, each
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi c
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_i^*(f) \in F(U_i)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            As a specific example, take the usual Grothendieck topology on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G: X \mapsto [X,R]
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Top
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to R
            belongs to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi j
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_*(F)
            iff it is
            %em locally
            constant; that is, for some open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U_i)_i
            of the domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f|U_i
            is constant.
          %p
            To make this precise in terms of the above definition, we need to understand the subobject classifier in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = Set^{C^{op}}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is simply the representing object for the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub: E^{op} \to Set
          %p
            which takes an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to the collection of subobjects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(F)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(F) \cong \hom_E(F, \Omega)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = \hom_C(-, c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Yoneda
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(\hom_C(-, c)) \cong \hom_{Set^{C^{op}}}(\hom_C(-, c), \Omega) \stackrel{Yoneda}{\cong} \Omega(c)
          %p
            In other words, we find that the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega: C^{op} \to Set
            is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi sieves
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi on
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega(c) = \{sieves \, on \, c\}
          %p
            Next, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is a Grothendieck topology on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-covering" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            (which we denote by
            = succeed "(" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(c)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(c) \hookrightarrow \Omega(c)
          %p
            and this inclusion is natural in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \hookrightarrow \Omega
          %p and again, by definition of subobject classifier, this subobject corresponds to a uniquely determined element
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j \in \hom_E(\Omega, \Omega)
          %p
            which is just the Lawvere–Tierney operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j: \Omega \to \Omega
          %p
            Conversely, any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j:\Omega\to\Omega
            determines a subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            a set of sieves on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+site"} small site
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              the Lawvere-Tierney topology on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = [C^{op}, Set]
              given by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationToCoveringSieves"}
              the
              %a{:href => "#SheafSubtoposes"} j-sheaves
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
              in the ordinary sense of Grothendieck topologies.
          %h3#ClosureOperation Relation to lex reflectors
          %p
            As discussed there,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+sheaves"} categories of sheaves
            are also characterized as being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
            of the given ambient topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi L
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh_j(\mathcal{E})
                  \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{}{\hookrightarrow}}
                  \\mathcal{E}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here we discuss explicit translations between the structure given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} reflector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and the corresponding Lawvere-Tierney topology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
            in a way that makes the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+%28in+computer+science%29"} monads (in computer science)
            most manifest.
          #ClosureOperatorOfReflection.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Given a reflector
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ♯
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi L
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp : \mathcal{E} \stackrel{L}{\to} Sh_j(\mathcal{E}) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{E}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong closure operator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                    %mo :
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    c_L : Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
                    \\,,
            %p
              by sending any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              classified by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A : X \to \Omega
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L(A)
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \sharp X
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \sharp X
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              This is well defined. Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L
              commutes with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+base"}> change of base
              ).
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, lemma A4.3.2
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              A family of functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Sub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(X) \to Sub(X)
              for all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              that commutes with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/change+of+base"} change of base
              is called a
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+closure+operation"} universal closure operation
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
              reflector
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              as above with induced closure operation
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              is given as the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi Ω
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                    %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j : \Omega \to \sharp \Omega \stackrel{\chi_{\sharp true}}{\to} \Omega
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo →
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \to \sharp \Omega
                  is the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi χ
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                        %mo :
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo →
                        %mi Ω
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_{\sharp true} : \sharp \Omega \to \Omega
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
                  of the result of applying
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} universal subobject
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mrow
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi true
                        %mo ♯
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo ♯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi true
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (* \stackrel{\sharp true}{\hookrightarrow} \sharp \Omega)
                        \:=
                        \\sharp (* \stackrel{true}{\hookrightarrow} \Omega)
                %p
                  (which is again a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
                  since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ♯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
                  preserves
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_A : X \to \Omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\chi_A}{\to}&amp; \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The pullback along the rightmost morphism is by definition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mo ♯
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp * \to \sharp \Omega
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; \sharp * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{\chi_A}{\to}&amp; \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} naturality
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} adjunction unit
              we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi χ
                                    %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ♯
                                  %msub
                                    %mi χ
                                    %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\to&amp; \sharp X
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\chi_A}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\sharp \chi_A}}
                    \\\
                    \\Omega &amp;\to&amp; \sharp \Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Using this in the remaining bottom morphism of our would-be pullback square we find that equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ♯
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; &amp;\to&amp; \sharp * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \sharp X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\sharp \chi_A}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
            %p
              needs to be a pullback diagram. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ♯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sharp
              preserves pullbacks we have that also the middle square in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ♯
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(A) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp A &amp;\to&amp; \sharp * = * &amp;\to&amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; \sharp X
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\sharp \chi_A}{\to}&amp;
                    \\sharp \Omega
                    \&amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp;
                    \\Omega
                    }
            %p
              is a pullback. But then also the left square is a pullback, by def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOperatorOfReflection"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Equivalently, by the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : \Omega \to \Omega
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+function"} characteristic function
              of the
              = succeed "-closure," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOperatorOfReflection"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * \to \Omega
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mo *
                            %mo =
                            %mo *
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo ♯
                            %mi Ω
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi χ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo ♯
                                    %mi true
                          %mtd
                            %mi Ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_L(*) &amp;\to&amp; \sharp * = * &amp;\to &amp; *
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Omega &amp;\to&amp; \sharp \Omega &amp;\stackrel{\chi_{\sharp true}}{\to} &amp; \Omega
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              In this form the statement appears in the proof of (
              %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone, Theorem A4.3.9
              ).
          %h2#enriched_generalization Enriched generalization
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic localizations and elementary toposes
                %strong 21
                (1980), no. 4, 393–401. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=606384"}> MR82g:18002
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_1980__21_4_393_0.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Sheaves of algebras for a commutative theory
                %strong 95
                (1981), no. 1, 3–19. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=628032"}> MR83c:18006
                )
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a small category enriched over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{\mathbf{T}}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theory"} commutative algebraic theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mtext Set
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},\text{Set}^{\mathbf{T}}]
            = succeed "-sieve" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mtext Set
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(-,x)\colon\mathcal{C}^{op}\rightarrow\text{Set}^{\mathbf{T}}
            = succeed "-topology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(x)
            of emptypage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
            \-sieves for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            He proves that there is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{\mathbf{T}}
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mtext Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},\text{Set}]
            which classifies subobjects in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mtext Set
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},\text{Set}^{\mathbf{T}}]
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                localizations of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mtext op
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mtext Set
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{\text{op}},\text{Set}^{\mathbf{T}}]
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
                \-topologies on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %li
              %p
                morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Ω
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j\colon\Omega_{\mathbf{T}}\rightarrow\Omega_{\mathbf{T}}
                satisfying the Lawvere-Tierney axioms for a topology
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modality"} modality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type+theory"} modal type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+%28in+programming+theory%29"} monad (in programming theory)
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion is introduced as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+modality"} geometric modality
            on p. 3 of
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantifiers and sheaves
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathunion.org/ICM/ICM1970.1/Main/icm1970.1.0329.0334.ocr.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Detailed discussion of Lawvere-Tierney operators as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+modalities"} geometric modalities
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Goldblatt
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Goldblatt"}> Robert Goldblatt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Grothendieck topology as geometric modality
          %p Textbook accounts include section V.1 of
          %ul
            %li#MacLaneMoerdijk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p (the notion of sheaves in section V.3, the sheafification functor in section V.3 and the relation to Grothendieck topologies in section V.4);
          %p and section A4.4 of
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#QuirinTabareau16
              Kevin Quirin, Nicolas Tabareau,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lawvere-Tierney sheafification in Homotopy Type Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://jfr.unibo.it/article/view/6232"} web
          %p
            The additive version of Lawvere-Tierney modular closure operators on categories of modules (as an additive version of a presheaf topos) – equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+topology"} Gabriel topology
            (=
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            \-enriched Grothendieck topology) has been studied (and the equivalence proven) several years before Lawvere and Tierney in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kim+Lin+Chew"}> Kim Lin Chew
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Closure operations in the study of rings of quotients
